        "# Update boxer (José)\n",
        "\n",
        "Updates one record of a boxer in the `boxers` table and shows the updated table.\n",
        "\n",
        "Run first the cells of `code_monkeys_boxers_db` (read_file, create_database, populate_table) so `boxers.db` exists.\n",
        "\n",
        "* `field`: only `wins`, `loses` or `draws` can be changed\n",
        "* `total_fights`: adjusted by the same difference as the record changed"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "WWNm8iWVtgxE"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "def update_boxer(boxer: str, field: str, new_value: int) -> pd.DataFrame | None:\n",
        "  \"\"\"\n",
        "  Update the wins, loses or draws of a boxer and show the updated table.\n",
        "\n",
        "  Looks up a boxer by name and replaces one of their records with a new value\n",
        "  (e.g. wins from 50 to 51). The total_fights of that boxer is adjusted by the\n",
        "  same difference, so the data stays consistent.\n",
        "\n",
        "  Args:\n",
        "    boxer (str): Name of the boxer, written as in the table (e.g. \"Mike Tyson\").\n",
        "    field (str): Record to change. Only \"wins\", \"loses\" or \"draws\" are valid.\n",
        "    new_value (int): New value for that record. Must be a whole number >= 0.\n",
        "  Returns:\n",
        "    pd.DataFrame | None: Pandas object with all the boxers after the change,\n",
        "      or None if nothing was updated.\n",
        "\n",
        "  Example:\n",
